                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Interesting concept. clunky execution.\nPhysics seem inconsistent - you can place items, and without moving them run the course twice, and the ring seems to end up in different locations.\nYou also have to get used to the weight and behavior of the different items - weight and momentum feels off.\n\nCycling between the items also seems to move them - I put two items close to each other, but the game didn't register a collision (items clipping into each other), yet once I cycled through the items, there's suddenly a collision.\n\nIt also seems that to pass some levels, you need to break the game's physics.\nMeaning have a board at 90 degrees, which stops it from moving, or clipping a board into a part of the level - creating a collision that doesn't register.\n\nThere are also a handful of small problems:\nI couldn't fully silence the audio, so there was always some noise in the background.\nThe game can become buggy with mouse movement, making the game feel sluggish - as if the mouse barely moves.\nThe levels also don't have a border - you can move items beyond the game's screen, and sometimes lose them, forcing you to exit the level and start again.",
